# The link-semantics matrix is complete: matrix.txt lists every row of plan 5.9.16 and every test of this directory, and each test does what its line says.
# matrix.txt has one line per row of plan 5.9.16 and per variant (rows that
# live elsewhere included: tests-p2 3.1's cases in 00-link, M19's p7 object
# test, M22's P2-C rows) and for the other tests of this directory, with
# the native result, the pipelines, the triples, the Phase 2 result and the
# milestones. Inputs/check-matrix.py, run with the repository root, checks
# the rules of M23.c and 5.17.12 (its docstring has them): every listed file
# exists and every .test here is listed; every '#! rows:' row has a line and
# every '#! obj-lto:' row lists obj and lto; every '#! p3-tests:' path is a
# test under msil/test that no line names; a 'UB' or 'link error' native
# result has a named diagnostic; a transcript line runs %{msil_prog} at the
# leg's levels on both x86_64 triples (or REQUIRES, or guards with
# '%if msil-triple-<os>', the one triple it names) under exactly its
# pipelines, against a generated .expected file, or a hand-written one on
# the triple of a '; rule <triple>:' clause (%{msil_expected_rule}); a
# diagnostic line fails to build at -O0 and at -O2 under each of its
# pipelines and FileChecks each level's output for the text with
# --implicit-check-not for 'LLVM ERROR' and 'PLEASE submit'; a P3 row (P3,
# P3-A, P3-B) pins its Phase 2 diagnostic or is 'untested' with a reason, no
# other row is untested, and no line names both a P3 label and a milestone
# from M24 to M35; pipeline-specific checks use msil-prog-pipeline, never
# msil-pipeline; no XFAIL line. The legs and gate rules need the legs
# (--legs, from lit-legs.ps1 -Describe), which the phase gates pass and this
# test does not. The self-test runs the checker on trees it builds, one good
# and one per rule broken. Plan 5.9.16, 5.12.7, 5.17.12, M23.c.
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/check-matrix.py --self-test | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=SELF
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/check-matrix.py %S/../../../.. | FileCheck %s
# SELF:  {{^}}self-test: the good tree: OK{{$}}
# SELF:  {{^}}self-test: [[N:[0-9]+]] of [[N]] checks passed{{$}}
# CHECK: {{^}}check-matrix: {{[0-9]+}} lines, {{[0-9]+}} tests: OK{{$}}
